y_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19883, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019QLYmZnzkfFzDhW2ekpNwc", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19883, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01GhZcgRSi1Ca1FuZFNokPzh", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20183, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GhZcgRSi1Ca1FuZFNokPzh", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20183, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GhZcgRSi1Ca1FuZFNokPzh", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 24803, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_018Xrg1zwM5ieLVFS5g6bhbj", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), error rate 18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving regions on different versions (us-east v2.3.0; us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A retry completed the rollback in all regions. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging before the production deploy), and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollback partway.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55403, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_018Xrg1zwM5ieLVFS5g6bhbj", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55403, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018Xrg1zwM5ieLVFS5g6bhbj", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58028, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01WQvpRFZxeis7YnxQviQNUw", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58328, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01WQvpRFZxeis7YnxQviQNUw", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58328, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WQvpRFZxeis7YnxQviQNUw", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63280, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- Before the rollback, v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate.\n- I chose v2.3.0 because it's the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Setting a version is safe to repeat, so I retried once and it finished in all regions.\n- After the retry, all regions are on v2.3.0 and healthy, with a 0.2% error rate.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. When I checked the incident list, it had been created anyway, so I didn't resend it and there's no duplicate page.\n- INC-0001 covers what went wrong, both rollback attempts and the current state. It also lists two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed. It was deployed to production even though its release candidate failed in staging.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback partway.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018Swm5gzufpZ8NgkHkGNg4D", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015s3ZBDFg8tUhNZx6R4RPyP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01RKCFkWuP5tN48W6ShmySAi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01QRUdZoHWwh4RsubHfcPVFC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Setting a version is safe to repeat, so I'll retry the rollback once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01HF2CVsVBXJa6E8ak5rGztL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019QLYmZnzkfFzDhW2ekpNwc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GhZcgRSi1Ca1FuZFNokPzh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018Xrg1zwM5ieLVFS5g6bhbj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), error rate 18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving regions on different versions (us-east v2.3.0; us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A retry completed the rollback in all regions. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging before the production deploy), and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollback partway.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WQvpRFZxeis7YnxQviQNUw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- Before the rollback, v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate.\n- I chose v2.3.0 because it's the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Setting a version is safe to repeat, so I retried once and it finished in all regions.\n- After the retry, all regions are on v2.3.0 and healthy, with a 0.2% error rate.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. When I checked the incident list, it had been created anyway, so I didn't resend it and there's no duplicate page.\n- INC-0001 covers what went wrong, both rollback attempts and the current state. It also lists two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed. It was deployed to production even though its release candidate failed in staging.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback partway.", "type": "text"}]}]}